msgctxt "@info"
msgid "The image contains pixels with zero alpha channel and non-zero color channels. Skissa has modified those pixels to have at least some alpha. The initial values will <i>not</i> be reverted on saving the image back.<br/><br/>This will hardly make any visual difference just keep it in mind."
msgstr "Tá picteilíní san íomhá le cainéal alfa nialasach agus bealaí datha neamh-nialasacha. Tá na picteilíní sin modhnaithe ag Skissa chun roinnt alfa a bheith acu ar a laghad. <i>Ní</i> aisiompófar na luachanna tosaigh nuair a shábhálfar an íomhá ar ais.<br/><br/>Is ar éigean a dhéanfaidh sé seo aon difríocht amhairc ach coinnigh i gcuimhne é."

msgctxt "@tooltip"
msgid "The image will be linearized first, and then encoded with SMPTE ST 428. Skissa always opens images like these as linear floating point, this option is there to reverse that"
msgstr "Déanfar an íomhá a líneáil ar dtús, agus ansin a ionchódú le SMPTE ST 428. Osclaíonn Skissa íomhánna mar seo i gcónaí mar snámhphointe líneach, tá an rogha seo ann chun é sin a aisiompú"

msgid "Layer \"%1\" has blending mode \"%2\" that has changed its behavior for CMYK color in Krita 5.2. Please check the result and consider enabling legacy \"Additive\" algorithm in Settings->Configure Skissa->General->Tools->CMYK blending mode"
msgstr "Tá modh cumasc \"%2\" ag an tsraith \"%1\" a d'athraigh a hiompar le haghaidh dath CMYK i Skissa 5.2. Seiceáil an toradh agus smaoinigh ar an sean-algartam \"Breiseach\" a chumasú i Socruithe->Cumraigh Skissa->Ginearálta->Uirlisí->Mód cumasc CMYK"

msgid "The file is too new for this version of Skissa (%1)."
msgstr "Tá an comhad ró-nua don leagan seo de Skissa (%1)."

